        <span>Buying Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Best Knee Braces for Walking</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        Most walkers with sore knees need light compression, not a rigid brace. The right choice depends on where it hurts and whether the knee feels unstable, so here are six braces matched to the problems walkers actually have, with what each listing confirms and what the guidelines say braces can and cannot do.
      </p>
      <p class="ed-answer"><strong>Short answer.</strong> Best Overall: <a href="#bauerfeind-genutrain">Bauerfeind GenuTrain</a>. Best Budget: <a href="#modvel-compression-sleeve">Modvel Compression Knee Sleeve (2-Pack)</a>. Best Hinged: <a href="#mcdavid-hinged-knee-brace">McDavid Hinged Knee Brace</a>.</p>

